Falsifies `file_allocation_table::directory::verification::every_slot_parses_as_its_bytes_say`.

The defect: the long-name test masks only the four low attribute bits, so a short entry with the
archive bit set beside read-only, hidden, system and volume label reads as a long-name piece and
its file disappears from the listing.

Expected to fail: the harness's `assert!(long)`.

diff --git a/crates/file_allocation_table/src/directory.rs b/crates/file_allocation_table/src/directory.rs
--- a/crates/file_allocation_table/src/directory.rs
+++ b/crates/file_allocation_table/src/directory.rs
@@ -26,7 +26,7 @@
 /// The low four attribute bits together, which mark a long-name slot.
 const LONG_NAME: u8 = READ_ONLY | HIDDEN | SYSTEM | VOLUME_ID;
 /// The attribute bits a long-name test looks at: the six the specification defines.
-const LONG_NAME_MASK: u8 = 0x3F;
+const LONG_NAME_MASK: u8 = 0x0F;
 /// The first name byte of a free slot.
 const FREE: u8 = 0xE5;
 /// The ordinal bit that marks a long name's last piece, which comes first on disk.
